WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.980
Anandpur, 1699.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.540
At the spring festival of Vaisakhi,
a crowd of Sikhs has gathered.

3
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.740
Guru Gobind Singh asks
a startling question:

4
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.730
who will give his head?

5
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.800
One by one, five men come forward,
from different castes and regions.

6
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.440
Nine years later, at
Nanded, the Guru is dying,

7
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.030
and he names no human successor.

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.700
So how did one Guru turn his
followers into the Khalsa,

9
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.410
and then end the line of human Gurus?

10
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.730
In this mission, you'll follow
the day the Khalsa began,

11
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.350
step by step.

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.030
Then you'll weigh up whether he
changed the Sikhism of Guru Nanak,

13
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.620
or carried it on.

14
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:44.690
Your mission: find out how
one Guru created the Khalsa,

15
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.990
then ended the line of human Gurus.
